# Normalise line endings across platforms.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF into the
# working tree while git stores LF in the index. The committed content is fine
# and `git diff` shows nothing, but Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"`, so
# `npm run format:check` fails on every file — 107 of them — for a problem that
# does not exist in the repository. That makes a real quality gate unusable on
# Windows and trains people to ignore it.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree on every platform, which is what
# Prettier, ESLint and the build all expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be EOL-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
